## Working conventions (confirmed/reinforced this session)
- Schema changes = vim/file edits. Data changes = `wp post`/`wp term`
  commands. Never conflate the two categories.
- Don't re-chown files in `acf-json/`; `chmod 666` the specific file if a
  write fails. Ownership will always revert to `www-data` on the next GUI
  save regardless — expected, not a bug.
- One deliberate GUI touch is acceptable and sometimes unavoidable (first
  Local JSON export, ACF's own field-group screen existing at all) — this
  is different from *habitual* GUI use, which remains avoided.
- User is deliberately building a personal CLI toolkit through real
  examples rather than upfront design — expect more scripts, expect some
  churn/replacement as patterns solidify.
